 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Variant 1: board is a non-empty rectangular list of integer rows (N rows, M columns) and 0 <= p < M. A path starts at (0, p), every move stays inside the grid, and the path ends as soon as it enters row N - 1 (when N = 1 the path is just the start cell). The score of a path is the sum of the board values of the cells it visits, including the start and the final cell. From (i, j) a move goes to (i + 1, j - 1), (i + 1, j) or (i + 1, j + 1); there is no special jump. Return the maximum score.",
  "provenance": [
